For example, querying the slot for KA-01-HH-9999 returns slot 2.
5. Time complexity
Let \(n\) be the parking lot capacity.
Operation	Data structure	Time complexity
Create parking lot	Initialise TreeSet	\(O(n\log n)\)
Find nearest slot	TreeSet.first()	\(O(\log n)\)
Remove available slot	TreeSet.remove()	\(O(\log n)\)
Park a car	TreeSet and HashMaps	\(O(\log n)\)
Leave a car	TreeSet and HashMaps	\(O(\log n)\)
Find slot by registration	HashMap	\(O(1)\) average
Display status	Iterate over occupied slots	\(O(n)\)
Search by colour	Scan occupied cars	\(O(n)\)

Note: TreeSet.first() itself is \(O(\log n)\) or better in the general Java API analysis convention; the practical implementation retrieves the first element efficiently. The overall parking operation is \(O(\log n)\).
