Both modes should use the same command-processing logic. This avoids duplicating the parking lot implementation.
7. What should you remember for an interview?
The most important design decision is choosing TreeSet<Integer> for the available slots. A regular queue would not work correctly because a slot that becomes free may have a smaller number than the slots already waiting.

For example, if available slots are {2, 4, 5} and slot 1 becomes free, the next car must get slot 1, not slot 2. A TreeSet handles this naturally.

The overall solution combines a sorted set for nearest-slot allocation, hash maps for fast lookups, and a Car class for object-oriented design.





























